# --------------------- gwf swi options ---------------------
# mf6 subpackage utl-tvg

block options
name zeta_filerecord
type record zeta fileout zetafile
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description

block options
name zeta
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname zeta keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to zeta.

block options
name fileout
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname file keyword
description keyword to specify that an output filename is expected next.

block options
name zetafile
type string
preserve_case true
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged false
optional false
longname file keyword
description name of the binary output file to write zeta information.  This zeta output file has the same format as the binary heads file.

block options
name tvg6_filerecord
type record tvg6 filein tvg6_filename
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description

block options
name tvg6
type keyword
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname tvg keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to a Time-Varying Grid (TVG) input file.  The behavior of TVG and a description of the input file is provided separately.

block options
name filein
type keyword
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname file keyword
description keyword to specify that an input filename is expected next.

block options
name tvg6_filename
type string
preserve_case true
in_record true
reader urword
tagged false
optional false
longname file name of TVG information
description name of the Time-Varying Grid (TVG) input file.  The TVG file is a generic file for specifying grid arrays that can change by stress period.  If the TVG file is specified in the options block, then the provided TVG file must have a SALTWATER\_HEAD auxiliary variable.  This SALTWATER\_HEAD auxiliary variable, which can vary during the simulation, will be assigned as the saltwater head used by the SWI Package. During solution of the freshwater flow equation, the provided SALTWATER\_HEAD array will remain fixed.  A common use case for providing SALTWATER\_HEAD in a TVG input file is to specify a sea level elevation that changes with time.  A description of the format of the TVG file is provided in a separate section.  If the TVG file is not specified, then the saltwater head is set to zero, or to the value specified with the SALTWATER\_HEAD option.

block options
name saltwater_head
type double precision
reader urword
optional true
longname saltwater head
description specified saltwater head value.  This saltwater head value will be assigned as the saltwater head used by the SWI Package. During solution of the freshwater flow equation the specified saltwater head will remain fixed.  A common use case for providing saltwater head is to set it equal to sea level, provided that sea level is not zero and does not change with time.  If not specified, and the TVG input option is not specified, then the default value for saltwater head is zero.  If the saltwater head option is specified and TVG input is also provided, then the saltwater head from the TVG input is used and the saltwater head option is ignored.
mf6internal hsalt_user

block options
name relative_density_difference
type double precision
reader urword
optional true
longname relative density difference
description dimensionless density difference between saltwater and freshwater, calculated as the saltwater density minus the freshwater density, divided by the freshwater density.  The value must be greater than zero.  If not specified, the default value is 0.025, which corresponds to a freshwater density of 1000. and a saltwater density of 1025.  The SWI Package uses this single dimensionless value instead of two densities because the interface position depends only on their ratio.  For a two-fluid simulation the same value must be specified for the freshwater model and the saltwater model; the SWI-SWI Exchange terminates with an error if the two differ.
mf6internal reldensdiff


block options
name dev_no_upstream_weighting
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname disable upstream weighting of the fluid-zone conductance
description keyword to disable upstream weighting of the freshwater or saltwater zone thickness in the intercell conductance.  This is a developer option for evaluating the weighting bias.  When specified, the fluid-zone saturated cell fractions of the two connected cells are averaged with the NPF cell-averaging method (harmonic by default, or as set with ALTERNATIVE\_CELL\_AVERAGING), the flow-term Newton derivatives are omitted, and the cross-fluid flow Newton terms of the SWI-SWI Exchange are disabled.  The storage Newton terms, which do not depend on the weighting, are retained.  The converged solution differs from the upstream-weighted solution only by the discretization of the intercell thickness.  Because the flow term is then solved by Picard iteration, two-fluid simulations with this option require backtracking in the Iterative Model Solution and typically need several times as many outer iterations; the harmonic-mean averaging cannot grow a fluid zone from zero thickness, so AMT-LMK or AMT-HMK averaging should be used.
mf6internal inoupstream
